-1. Each round — the first and every one after a fix — is `keryx review start` on the PR's current head, then `review-orchestrator` from that package. `review start` finds the previous round itself (local package, git history, the PR's round block, the flow package) and, when the previous reviewed head is an ancestor, reviews the delta: fix changes with a small roster (logic, regression, the findings' authors, security-code when a security finding is attached, the verifier) and the prior findings attached, new changes as round 1, unchanged code carried with its dispositions. Never pass a whole-branch range or `--all` per round; `<package>/round.json` records the round, its source and its mode.
